# Review routing. Every path has the same owner today; the file exists so that
# ownership is declared rather than inferred, and so a second maintainer is a
# one-line change rather than a new convention.
#
# The default branch ruleset deliberately does NOT require code-owner review.
# That is not an oversight: CODEOWNERS resolves to users and teams, a GitHub App
# can never be one, and this repository's Dependabot policy merges eligible
# bumps on the automation App's approval. Turning require_code_owner_review on
# would leave every App-approved pull request sitting at REVIEW_REQUIRED with
# nothing failing — the approval posts, auto-merge stays armed, and the merge
# never fires. If a second human joins and code-owner review becomes worth
# requiring, note that a ruleset cannot scope that requirement by changed
# path — its conditions match refs, and only the patterns in this file decide
# which paths need an owner's review. Requiring it while `*` owns everything
# therefore holds every bot pull request; narrowing these patterns to paths
# Dependabot never bumps is the only way to have both, and the paths worth
# owning are largely the ones it bumps. Verify a bot pull request still merges
# before relying on any of it.

